Krita Nova 34 - HSV Adjustment per color range, like Photoshop's Hue/Saturation

Filter > Adjust > HSV/HSL Adjustment (Ctrl+U) gets a "Colors:" box above the
sliders: Master (all colors, as before) or one color range - Reds, Yellows,
Greens, Cyans, Blues, Magentas (Alt+2 .. Alt+8, as in Photoshop). The three
sliders show and change the chosen range; every range keeps its own values,
and they all apply together. Reset resets every range.

How a range applies (kis_hsv_adjustment.cpp, KisHSVAdjustment): its hue /
saturation / value-lightness-intensity-luma adjustments are added to Master's,
weighted by how close the pixel's own hue is to the range's center (0, 60,
120, 180, 240, 300 degrees): fully within 15 degrees, fading out over the next
30 (Photoshop's default range widths), so neighbouring ranges blend. Grays are
in no range. The result goes through the existing HSV/HSL/HSI/HSY formulas
(compatibility mode too).

Color ranges are for the hue based models (HSV, HSL, HSI, HSY) without
Colorize; for YUV or Colorize the box is disabled and Master is used.

Configuration: "h", "s", "v" stay Master's (old presets and documents load as
before); the ranges are "h_1".."v_6" (1 = Reds ... 6 = Magentas), and "range"
is the one shown. The transformation gets them as "rangeH", "rangeS", "rangeV"
(six values each, only when one is not zero).
